okf_version: "1.0"
task: "restart_session: codex-remote restarts its app-server too, with a new workspace MCP launch and the same thread; every path waits for the running turn and shows a notice; Claude and plain Codex also renew their workspace MCP launch."
requested: "User, 2026-10-10: '고칠 내용: restart_session이 codex-remote에서 app-server까지 다시 띄우게 합니다. 이때 MCP를 다시 만들고 같은 thread로 resume합니다. 안전장치: 진행 중인 turn이 있으면 끝날 때까지 기다리고, 재시작 공지를 띄웁니다. Claude·일반 Codex 경로도 MCP를 다시 만들게 합니다. 검증: e2e로 확인합니다. 새 manifest, 프로필 6개·도구 12개, 같은 thread id, goal과 SSE 유지.'"
before: "restart_poll claimed the request and the transports killed the CLI at once (mid-turn). codex-remote only restarted the TUI; the app-server, its MCP servers and the workspace MCP launch stayed. Claude/Codex relaunched with the same --mcp-config / -c mcp_servers.* arguments and the same launch directory."
changes:
  turn_wait: "runtime_session_restart.RuntimeSessionRestartControl.incoming(busy, notify): the request is claimed at once (the request file's 300 s TTL no longer matters) and held while a turn runs, re-checking every 0.5 s, up to CIEL_RUNTIME_SESSION_RESTART_TURN_WAIT_SECONDS (default 900 s). Notices: '[ciel-runtime] 세션 재시작 요청을 받았습니다 — 진행 중인 turn이 끝나면 재시작합니다 (...)' when it waits, '[ciel-runtime] 세션을 재시작합니다 — MCP를 다시 만들고 같은 대화로 이어집니다 (...)' when it goes. Turn signal: control.busy (codex-remote: the channel client's active turn, CodexAppServerChannelInjector.turn_running; a goal between turns does not count) or the console proxy's own input_busy (transcript: active tool call or active turn). The direct transport (no console proxy) has no turn signal and restarts at once, as before."
  proxy: "channel_terminal_proxy._runtime_session_restart_requested passes busy=polling.input_busy and a notify that writes to the console (Windows ConPTY/console-input and POSIX pty)."
  mcp_renewal: "workspace_mcp.WorkspaceMcpLaunchService.renew (prepare a new launch from the reloaded config, then finish the old one; on failure keep the old one) and workspace_mcp.renew_launch_command (swap the --mcp-config projection paths or the contiguous -c mcp_servers.* run; add/remove when one side is empty). Used by run_claude (renew_claude_mcp, same router MCP injection as the first launch), run_codex (renew_codex_mcp) and run_codex_app_server (relaunch)."
  codex_remote: "codex_app_server_session.CodexRemoteTuiSession loops over _run_once (server + channel client + TUI). On a restart request it stops all three, calls relaunch(request) from run_codex_app_server (session backup, renewed MCP launch, the restart-complete notice) and starts the server and TUI again with the same thread (resume=false: a new conversation). The session advertises relaunches_server; CodexAppServerLaunchServices gained restart ports and routing.router_log (codex_launch_assembly wires them)."
  tool_text: "restart_session description now says the turn finishes first, MCP servers start anew and codex-remote restarts its app-server on the same thread."
tests: "tests/test_session_restart_turn_wait.py (13: wait/notices/limit/session signal/no signal/reset/proxy; renew_launch_command for Claude and Codex; renew service), test_runtime_session_restart +1 (Claude restart gets a new MCP launch, both launch dirs gone at exit), test_codex_app_server_session +3 (server relaunched with the renewed command, same thread, new token; resume=false starts fresh). Groups: runtime 402 OK, router 1188 OK, channel 457 OK, unit 1817 with 1 error = test_tool_guard writing a temp file: '[Errno 28] No space left on device' (C: had 156 MB free) - environment. ruff clean. Router 9611 healthy throughout."
e2e:
  harness: "evidence/e2e_restart.py <mode> (+ e2e_mcp_server.py: stdio MCP server, 3 tools, logs each start; e2e_restart_console.py: detached console watcher that keeps screens showing the notices; console_driver.py, shot_title.ps1). Isolated config/CODEX_HOME on G:, unique ports, CIEL_RUNTIME_TEST_ISOLATED, stub upstream (provider vllm). Turn 2 sleeps 25 s at the stub; restart_session is called through /ca/mcp 2 s into it. SSE clients on /ca/chat/stream and /ca/events/stream for the whole run; send_message before and after the restart."
  codex_remote: "e2e-codex-remote (run 13:42-13:44): restart claimed 13:43:11 (request 1791657791.55), waiting notice on screen 13:43:11, slow reply at the stub 1791657814.33 (13:43:34), 'starting' notice 13:43:35, codex_remote_session_restart 13:43:38. Manifest b0fdbf49... -> a67f15bf... (old removed: workspace_mcp_launch_removed reason=normal_exit; workspace_mcp_launch_renewed). MCP server pid 24644 -> 88012 after the restart. mcpServerStatus/list before and after: e2e-tools connected, tools [e2e_clock, e2e_echo, e2e_pid]. Thread 01a1271f-af4d-7fe2-96a4-17d5b6b4595e before, in codex_remote_app_server_ready resume= after, and in the TUI resume. Goal (set paused over the app-server) after: same objective 'E2E-GOAL-KEEP survive the restart', status paused; the resumed TUI asks 'Resume paused goal?' and shows 'Goal paused' (shots/04-turn-3.png). Turn 3's request carries turn 1, turn 2 and the restart notice. SSE: both connections never closed; chat stream delivered E2E-SSE-BEFORE and E2E-SSE-AFTER, events stream 13 data events after the restart."
  codex: "e2e-codex (13:44-13:46): claimed 13:45:13, waiting notice 13:45:14, slow reply 1791657936.47 (13:45:36), restart 13:45:37; manifest 20abf250... -> ffa95f2c...; MCP pid 7532 -> 76308; model tool list identical (11). Same conversation: one rollout file (01a12721-7e79-...) holding wakes pending_ids=1,2 before and 3,4 after (plain Codex receives channel input as '[ciel-wake] pending_ids=N' markers, so the stub only sees the current turn's text). SSE both open; chat stream had data after."
  claude: "e2e-claude (13:55-13:58): claimed 13:58:01, waiting notice 13:58:01, slow reply 1791658704.16 (13:58:24), restart 13:58:25 (claude_session_socket_renewed, workspace_mcp_launch_renewed 312b7bea... -> 777667a9...); MCP pid 63132 -> 79020; the model's 44 tools identical before/after (mcp: ciel-runtime-router 11, duckduckgo 2, e2e-tools 3, web_fetch 1); turn 3's history has turns 1, 2 and the restart notice. SSE both open. Claude used the default ~/.claude; its E2E transcript folder G--ciel-e2e-restart-claude-ws was deleted afterwards."
observations:
  - "Each mcpServerStatus/list call from a second app-server client started one more e2e-tools process (pid 17580 at the 'before' query, 34008 at the 'after' query). Seen, cause not investigated; not part of the restart path."
  - "The codex-remote TUI showed 'OpenAI Codex (v0.162.0)' while 'codex --version' in this shell prints 0.158.0 - two installs on PATH; not investigated."
open_question: "'프로필 6개·도구 12개': not identified in the code or the user's message. Measured instead: this E2E's workspace MCP (1 server, 3 tools) and the Claude router MCP (11 tools) are the same before and after. Asked the user what the 6/12 count."
not_verified:
  - "A live session (no restart of live sessions without approval)."
  - "The direct transport (no console proxy) - it restarts at once, no turn signal."
  - "POSIX pty path - code path covered by unit tests only."
not_done: "Not committed, pushed or deployed."
